  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Nagiyev and Viktor have a heated argument in the office about the restaurant's budget. Nagiyev wants to save money by firing the most expensive kitchen staff.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Я должен уволить твоих поваров.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты совсем сошёл с ума?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Они слишком дорого стоят.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Это почти полмиллиона каждый месяц.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты не можешь их увольнять.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это лучшая команда в Москве.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Дешевле найти новых людей.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Какая разница, кто режет морковь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это моя команда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Если ты их уволишь, ты потеряешь меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Витя, просто сядь и успокойся.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хорошо, разбирайтесь сами.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А я пока увольняюсь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Подожди, мы всё решим.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let us break down this interaction.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Я должен уволить твоих поваров.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I must fire your cooks.' Notice how 'I' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'cooks'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты совсем сошёл с ума?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Have you gone completely crazy?' Notice how 'you' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'mind'. Then Dmitry responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Они слишком дорого стоят.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'They cost too much.' Dmitry links 'they' directly with 'too' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Это почти полмиллиона каждый месяц.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is almost half a million every month.' Notice how 'this' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'month'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты не можешь их увольнять.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You cannot fire them.' Notice how 'you' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'to fire'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это лучшая команда в Москве.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is the best team in Moscow.' Chef Viktor combines 'this' with 'Moscow' in a natural Russian turn of phrase. Then Dmitry responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Дешевле найти новых людей.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is cheaper to find new people.' Dmitry links 'cheaper' directly with 'to find' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Какая разница, кто режет морковь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What difference does it make who cuts carrots?' The question opens with the interrogative word for 'who' and builds toward 'carrot'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это моя команда!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is my team!' Notice how 'this' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'team'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Если ты их уволишь, ты потеряешь меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'If you fire them, you will lose me.' Chef Viktor links 'if' directly with 'you' to express the thought clearly. Then Dmitry responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Витя, просто сядь и успокойся.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vitya, just sit and calm down.' Notice how 'Vitya' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'calm down'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хорошо, разбирайтесь сами.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Alright, sort it out yourselves.' The reflexive ending on the verb for 'to understand well' turns the action back onto the subject.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А я пока увольняюсь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And I am quitting in the meantime.' Notice the reflexive ending on the verb for 'quit', which directs the action back onto the subject.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "nagiyev",
      "t": "Подожди, мы всё решим.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Wait, we will solve everything.' Notice how 'wait' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'will sort out'. Now let us listen to the conversation again without interruption.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
